# Financial Reporting
# Report setup wizard. (The older pages of the module still have English text in the code; they move here over time.)
FinRepWizTitle = Report setup wizard
FinRepWizMenu = Report wizard
FinRepWizIntro = The wizard builds an income statement as a Dolibarr <b>personalised report</b> (Accounting > Setup > Personalized groups). A report is a list of <b>groups of accounts</b> (for example Revenue, Cost of sales) and <b>formula lines</b> that combine groups by their codes (for example Gross profit = REVENUE - COGS). It goes through the report one section at a time: you check each group, set which account numbers it takes, and add your own groups if you want.
FinRepWizIntroSign = Every line is shown as a <b>positive amount</b>: income as credit − debit, expenses as debit − credit. So formulas <b>subtract</b> expenses, as on a printed income statement.
FinRepWizIntroWrites = Saving creates a <b>new</b> personalised report. Existing reports, the chart of accounts and the ledger are not changed. A report built by the wizard can be deleted here.
FinRepWizCaution = This layout reflects our understanding of the rules for %s on %s. Rules change, and your situation may differ. Check the layout with your accountant before relying on it for statutory or tax reporting.
